        "title": "Bifurcations",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A bifurcation is a **qualitative change in the phase portrait** as a parameter crosses a critical\nvalue: fixed points appear or annihilate, swap stability, or spawn limit cycles. These are exactly\nthe events linearization cannot resolve — they happen precisely where an eigenvalue's real part hits\nzero (Ch. 02). The astonishing fact, the reason the subject is teachable, is that near such an event\nthe dynamics collapse onto a **normal form**: one of a handful of universal low-order equations."
    }
